# #1075: Auto theme follows an OS Light/Dark switch. `appearance-set` plays
# the switch through the handler gpui's window appearance observer calls on
# macOS (`Docxy::os_appearance_changed`); the observer registration in
# `open_docxy_window` is not exercised by this case — it is checked by review
# and on macOS. Auto follows the switch both ways, a chosen Light/Dark
# ignores it, and back on Auto the current OS appearance applies at once
# (`applied` is the drawn mode, read after the call). The tests share one
# instance, as the runner runs them;
# the second sets the appearance before every assert that reads it, so
# neither test depends on the machine's real appearance.

test auto theme follows an OS Light/Dark switch
  open copy:../fixtures/basic.docx
  call theme-set {"theme":"auto"}
  call appearance-set {"appearance":"light"}
  assert reply.applied is light
  call appearance-set {"appearance":"dark"}
  assert reply.theme is auto
  assert reply.resolved is dark
  assert reply.applied is dark
  shot window
  call appearance-set {"appearance":"light"}
  assert reply.applied is light
test a chosen theme ignores the OS switch
  open copy:../fixtures/basic.docx
  call theme-set {"theme":"light"}
  call appearance-set {"appearance":"dark"}
  assert reply.applied is light
  call theme-set {"theme":"auto"}
  assert reply.resolved is dark
  call appearance-set {"appearance":"light"}
  call theme-set {"theme":"dark"}
  call appearance-set {"appearance":"light"}
  assert reply.applied is dark
  call theme-set {"theme":"auto"}
  call-error appearance-set {"appearance":"dim"} => unknown appearance 'dim'
